If you build and distribute ANY binary from this repository (boot image,
kernelsu.ko, Manager APK, ...), you MUST accompany it with the corresponding
source for that exact build and both license texts. A private repository is
only suitable for keeping your own build artifacts; it cannot be used to
distribute a closed-source derivative publicly.

KernelSU v1.0+ only supports GKI 2.0 (kernel 5.10+). Kernel 4.19 is within
the official 4.14+ backport range but is still non-GKI: upstream provides NO
boot image for it. This repository contains NO flashable root package and
makes NO claim that a prebuilt adapted APK exists.
